{
  "case_id": "2009-08-304",
  "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b787c5e680-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Graham County Soil and Water Conservation District (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b787c5e680-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If this Court were to hold that a relator can simply copy a State report or a State criminal indictment and then proceed with a qui tam action, there will be a proliferation of opportunistic qui tam actions brought under this statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Graham County Soil and Water Conservation District (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b787c5e680-0000-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Such construction of the statute would have a devastating effect upon States, local governments, and the Federal fisc."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Graham County Soil and Water Conservation District (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b787c5e680-0000-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government certainly argues that it would result in State and local governments immunizing themselves from qui tam liability."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b787c5e680-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: In your view, must an administrative report be a report that is generated by some government unit? Could it be a report by the administration of a university, for example?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b787c5e680-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you tell me just as a practical matter, suppose -- suppose the county says, you know, we found out that we were defrauded by this contractor, and it sues the contractor. But its suit doesn't cover really all of the damages, only half of it. Can a qui tam action then be commenced for the portion that the county isn't seeking? I mean, how does that work?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2009-08-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b787c5e680-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first category is clearly adjudicative in nature. The second is non-adjudicative. And the third category is -- is news media and stands on its own."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b787c5e680-0001-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As I think the discussion this morning illustrates, the Federal nature of the second category, the phrase that is directly at issue in this case, is self-evident from the text. The terms congressional and GAO are Federal and under the doctrine or canon of construction noscitur a sociis --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-304",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b787c5e680-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I just want to get your expertise on this, because you have probably read the legislative history of the 1986 amendment. All right, am I right in thinking this? If I go back and read it -- which I will -- I will discover, not once in this entire 1986 history anywhere, House, Senate or conference, does the word State appear in any relevant context?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-304",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b787c5e680-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Could you be more specific when you say that Congress had in mind? Just so I know what you are talking about?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-304",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b787c5e680-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But why can't it -- why can't it protect itself if these reports are in its possession? How are they any more in the -- or less in the government's possession than articles in the news media, than State, criminal, civil, and administrative hearings?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-304",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "04b787c5e680cdeb6ea0618ec7ff7a293931d1efbec89a27f4372ebaa47871c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b787c5e680-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:04 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
